# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Shows ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your shows library. Anything you put
# here gets silently dropped from output/shows/warnings.json on every run.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to `ignored/shows.yaml` (drop the `.example` suffix).
#      The real `shows.yaml` is gitignored so your personal decisions don't
#      end up in version control.
#   2. Add path prefixes below — one per line.
#   3. Re-run `npm run shows`. Matching warnings disappear from the output.
#
# How matching works: each entry is a path PREFIX. A warning whose `path`
# starts with one of these (slash- or end-of-string-bounded) is silenced.
# Matching is case-insensitive and forward-slash-normalized, so it works on
# Windows and macOS/Linux libraries alike.
#
# Get the paths to add from output/shows/warnings.json and
# output/shows/validation-warnings.json.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence a whole show you can't fix
# (Use this when a show has known missing episodes — never released on disc,
# culled by the rights holder, etc. — and you don't want to see
# warn_episode_gaps / warn_tmdb_episode_count noise every run.)
# - HD/Channel 4 Catchup (2024)
# - HD/Some Reality Show (2020)


# Silence one season
# (The rest of the show's warnings stay live, but everything under this
# specific season folder is dropped.)
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
# - UHD/Star Trek Enterprise (2001)/Season 4


# Silence one episode
# (Pin-point: just one file. Useful when one episode has a legitimate quality
# outlier you've decided to accept.)
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 1/Some Show (2020) - S01E05.mp4


# Silence a whole category folder
# (Drops EVERY warning under this folder.)
# - Other HD
# - Other SD
